prompt:
You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method has_close_elements(numbers: seq<real>, threshold: real) returns (res: bool)
  requires threshold >= 0.0
  ensures res ==> exists i: int, j: int :: 0 <= i < |numbers| && 0 <= j < |numbers| && i != j && (if numbers[i] - numbers[j] < 0.0 then numbers[j] - numbers[i] else numbers[i] - numbers[j]) < threshold
  ensures !res ==> (forall i: int, j: int :: 1 <= i < |numbers| && 0 <= j < i ==>  (if numbers[i] - numbers[j] < 0.0 then numbers[j] - numbers[i] else numbers[i] - numbers[j]) >= threshold)


{

  res := false;
  var idx: int := 0;
  while idx < |numbers| && !res
    invariant 0 <= idx <= (|numbers|) + 1
    invariant !res
    invariant forall i: int, j: int :: 0 <= i < idx && 0 <= j < i ==> (if numbers[i] - numbers[j] < 0.0 then numbers[j] - numbers[i] else numbers[i] - numbers[j]) >= threshold
  {
    var idx2: int := 0;
    while idx2 < idx && !res
      invariant 0 <= idx <= |numbers|
      invariant 0 <= idx2 <= idx
      invariant !res
      invariant forall j: int :: 0 <= j < idx2 ==> (if numbers[idx] - numbers[j] < 0.0 then numbers[j] - numbers[idx] else numbers[idx] - numbers[j]) >= threshold
    {

      var distance :=  (if numbers[idx2] - numbers[idx] < 0.0 then numbers[idx] - numbers[idx2] else numbers[idx2] - numbers[idx]);
      if distance < threshold  {
        res := true;
        return;
      }

      idx2 := idx2 + 1;
    }
    idx := idx + 1;
  }
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(14,81): Error: index out of range

program.dfy(14,129): Error: index out of range

program.dfy(14,145): Error: index out of range

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 3 errors

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
For the error at line 14: At initial state: threshold = 0, |numbers| = 2283. At a program state: res = false. At a program state: idx = 0.
For the error at line 14: At initial state: numbers[2437] = 0, threshold = 0, |numbers| = 2438. At a program state: res = false. At a program state: idx = 0.
For the error at line 14: At initial state: numbers[8098] = 0, threshold = 0, |numbers| = 8099. At a program state: res = false. At a program state: idx = 0.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

